; Source: HSPICE User Guide: Basic Simulation and Analysis, H-2013.03,
; chapter 10, "Defining Tabular Data", "Expected Output": at 11 the first and
; fourth outputs are expected high and the others low; at 20 the first two
; high; at 30 only the first; at 35 the first two are "don't care" and the
; last two low. The RADIX line is added to declare the four vectors.
RADIX 1111
IO OOOO
; start of tabular section data
11.0 1001
20.0 1100
30.0 1000
35.0 xx00
